# Testing

## What to test
- ✅ Unit: domain usecases, mappers, repositories (mock sources)
- ✅ Widget: key screens, error/loading states, navigation triggers
- ✅ Integration: critical user flows (auth, checkout, core workflows)

## Riverpod testing
- ✅ Prefer overriding providers in tests:
  - `ProviderScope(overrides: [...])` for widget tests
  - `ProviderContainer(overrides: [...])` for unit-style provider tests
- ✅ Test `AsyncValue` states explicitly (loading/data/error)

## Conventions
- ✅ Arrange/Act/Assert structure
- ✅ Test names describe behavior, not implementation
- ✅ Use fakes/fixtures for deterministic tests

## Mocking
- ✅ Mock external boundaries (API/local storage/time)
- ✅ Avoid mocking Flutter framework internals

## NEVER
- ❌ Write tests that depend on real network
- ❌ Skip error-state tests
